-- Audit 2026-11-16 (findings M4, M5, M9): photos and links.
-- Photo rule (owner, 2026-11-11): only the event's own photo. Cleared here: the same picture used for unrelated events in different places or for different homes, logos, a 2016 site banner,
-- a business-licence screenshot, a flyer, a list-page thumbnail, a Canva design. The card then shows the stock photo for its type. Every change is guarded by the old image, so a newer edit is never overwritten.
-- Kept after looking at them: portrait photos in the 0.55-2.8 ratio range (ventura-stpat-parade 582x900, g19-festival-of-trees-oaks, grok-krampus-rumpus 2400x3000) are allowed by the rule in docs/sweep-methods.md.
-- http image links: visitsantaclarita.com, irvineparkrailroad.com and sawdustartfestival.org all serve the same file over https (200 image checked), so only the scheme changes; hbturkeywobble.com's file is a 1080x1080 logo (cleared);
--   the two Downey events shared one 2019 squarespace graphic over http (cleared).
